,552,555,558,561,564,567],{"id":496,"title":497},"howto.get-started","Get started — a first project",{"id":499,"title":500},"howto.first-drum-beat","Program a first drum beat",{"id":502,"title":503},"howto.first-bassline","Record a bassline live",{"id":505,"title":506},"howto.first-chords","Add chords on steps",{"id":508,"title":509},"howto.first-punch-in","Perform with punch-in FX",{"id":511,"title":512},"howto.enable-velocity","Make the keyboard velocity-sensitive",{"id":514,"title":515},"howto.control-synth-midi","Play an external synth over MIDI",{"id":517,"title":518},"howto.control-cv-synth","Play an analog synth with CV and gate",{"id":520,"title":521},"howto.sync-drum-machine","Sync a vintage drum machine",{"id":523,"title":524},"howto.sync-pocket-operator","Sync a pocket operator",{"id":526,"title":527},"howto.external-effect","Loop an external effect pedal",{"id":529,"title":530},"howto.midi-keyboard","Play the OP-XY from a MIDI keyboard",{"id":532,"title":533},"howto.audio-interface","Use an audio interface with the OP-XY",{"id":535,"title":536},"howto.pitchbend-modulation","Use the pitchbend strip as a modulator",{"id":538,"title":539},"howto.back-up-projects","Back up projects to a computer",{"id":541,"title":542},"howto.load-samples","Load samples from a computer",{"id":544,"title":545},"howto.song-with-brain","Sketch a song fast with the brain",{"id":547,"title":548},"howto.song-from-scenes","Build a song from scenes",{"id":550,"title":551},"howto.loop-one-scene","Loop one scene",{"id":553,"title":554},"howto.sidechain-duck","Make a track pump with the kick (duck)",{"id":556,"title":557},"howto.pluck","Turn a sound into a pluck",{"id":559,"title":560},"howto.pad-swell","A pad that swells in and fades slowly",{"id":562,"title":563},"howto.wobble","A filter wobble in time with the beat",{"id":565,"title":566},"howto.acid-bass","A squelchy acid bass",{"id":568,"title":569},"howto.slice-a-loop","Sample a loop and play it in slices"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":269,"prev":23,"next":271,"titles":274,"firmware":88},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":16,"status":17,"firmware":18,"facts":24,"procedures":155,"parameters":214,"related":215,"body":218,"sources":219,"official_url":39,"controls":246},"hardware.layout","Panel layout",[5,6,7,8,9],"top panel","front panel","control map","where is a key","buttons and knobs","hardware",0,"knowledge/manual/units/hardware/layout.md",{"modes":14,"screens":15},[],[],"A map of the top panel — mode keys, module keys, track and step keys, transport, keyboard, function keys, encoders, screen and sockets — and the names this manual uses for each.","current",{"min":19,"changed_in":20,"guide_version":22,"verified_on":23},"1.0.9",[21],"1.0.36","1.1.15",null,[25,30,33,36,41,45,48,51,55,59,63,66,69,74,78,81,84,90,93,96,100,104,108,112,116,120,124,128,132,136,140,144,148,151],{"id":26,"text":27,"source":28,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":29},"grid","Seen from above, the controls sit on a grid of 17 columns and 6 rows. The top two rows hold the speaker, the volume knob, the screen and the four encoders; keys fill the four rows below.","docs/research/50-hardware-ui.md#14-the-grid-plan-view","measured",{"id":31,"text":32,"source":28,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":29},"rows","Row three runs mode keys, `M1`…`M4`, then `T1`…`T8`; row four is `step 1`…`step 16`; the bottom two rows put `record`, `play`, `stop` above `[-]`, `[+]`, `shift` on the left, with the keyboard to their right.",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":28,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":29},"right-column","The rightmost column holds `sample`, `com`, `player` and `bar`, top to bottom; `project` and `tempo` sit just below the volume knob.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":39,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"mode-keys","Four keys pick the main mode: `instrument` for the eight sound tracks, `auxiliary` for the eight utility tracks (brain, punch-in FX, external gear, tape, send effects), `arrange` for patterns, scenes and songs, and `mix` for levels, pans, EQ and the master compressor.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#main-modes","official",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":44,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"module-keys","The keys printed 1 to 4 directly under the screen are the module keys, written `M1`…`M4`. Each opens one page of the current mode, and the four encoders then edit what that page shows.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#modules",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":44,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"arrange-no-modules","Arrange is the only main mode without module pages.",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":44,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"shift-layer","Some pages keep a second set of parameters on a shift layer, reached by holding `shift`.",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":54,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"track-keys","The eight track keys under the encoders choose which track you edit — an instrument track in instrument mode, an auxiliary track in auxiliary mode.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#track-buttons",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":58,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"step-keys","The sixteen step keys across the middle form the step sequencer, the grid you program notes and sounds into.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#sequencer",{"id":60,"text":61,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"transport","`record` arms recording of notes and knob moves, `play` starts playback and `stop` halts it.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#transport-controls",{"id":64,"text":65,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"play-again","Pressing `play` again during playback jumps back to the start of the pattern.",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"stop-again","A second press of `stop` cuts off every note and sound that is still ringing.",{"id":70,"text":71,"source":72,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":73},"stop-on-1-1-33","On OS 1.1.33 one `stop` stops playback, and `play` then starts from the beginning — a pattern from its first step, a song from its first scene — with a MIDI start, never a continue. A 1.1.25 tutorial says so and a 1.2 one shows it. What the step keys show after the stop is not yet checked on 1.1.x.","docs/research/74-behaviour-os-check.md#1-stop-and-play-the-known-conflict","community-verified",{"id":75,"text":76,"source":77,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":73},"stop-pauses","In tutorial videos on OS 1.0.x, unlike 1.1.33, one `stop` during playback pauses — the position is kept and the step keys stay on the bar the playhead stopped in — and `play` carries on from there; a song carries on in its scene.","docs/research/73-overnight-run.md#log",{"id":79,"text":80,"source":77,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":73},"stop-rewinds","In the same videos a `stop` while already stopped goes back to the start, so `stop → stop` and then `play` starts from the top.",{"id":82,"text":83,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"octave-keys","`[-]` and `[+]` move the keyboard one octave down or up; several pages give them other jobs.",{"id":85,"text":86,"source":87,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":88,"confidence":89},"octave-popup","On an instrument page, `[-]` and `[+]` bring up a small white card low in the middle of the screen, with a mini keyboard and the octave offset in thin digits (+0, +1, −1, −3 …). On the external CV page the offset appears inside the meter card instead.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#212-octave-popup","1.1.33","verified",{"id":91,"text":92,"source":87,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":73},"octave-popup-timing","The octave card stays about 1.08 s after the last press of `[-]` or `[+]`, then disappears from one frame to the next, without a fade (tutorial videos, OS 1.0.x).",{"id":94,"text":95,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"shift-key","`shift` does nothing alone: held with another key it opens that key's secondary function or page.",{"id":97,"text":98,"source":99,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"keyboard","The two-octave keyboard of 24 keys lies right of the transport keys, below the step keys.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#keyboard",{"id":101,"text":102,"source":103,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"naturals","Every white key carries the icon of one step component; counted from the left they are `natural 1`…`natural 14`.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/step-components#adding-step-components-to-a-sequence",{"id":105,"text":106,"source":107,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"accidentals","The ten black keys double as number keys, marked 1–9 and 0 from the left; this manual calls them `accidental 1`…`accidental 0`.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/step-components#step-components-ref-table",{"id":109,"text":110,"source":111,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"sample-key","`sample` (top right corner) starts sampling from any screen.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#sample",{"id":113,"text":114,"source":115,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"project-key","`project` opens the list of projects, where you create, open and manage them.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#projects",{"id":117,"text":118,"source":119,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"tempo-key","`tempo` sets the song speed, the swing and the metronome.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#tempo",{"id":121,"text":122,"source":123,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"com-key","`com` is the hub for system settings, wired and wireless connections and output routing.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#com",{"id":125,"text":126,"source":127,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"player-key","`player` turns the notes of a track into arpeggios, chords and other note effects.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#players",{"id":129,"text":130,"source":131,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"bar-key","`bar` lengthens the sequence and holds sequence-wide settings such as quantisation.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#bar",{"id":133,"text":134,"source":135,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"volume","The volume knob is at the top left, next to the speaker.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#volume",{"id":137,"text":138,"source":139,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"encoders","The four encoders shade from dark to light: dark gray, mid gray, light gray and white. This manual calls them `E1`, `E2`, `E3` and `E4` in that order.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/layout#encoders",{"id":141,"text":142,"source":143,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"pitchbend","The pitchbend strip on the lower left edge responds to pressure — push its left end to bend down, its right end to bend up.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/hardware-overview#speaker-volume-pitchbend",{"id":145,"text":146,"source":147,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"sockets","The right side carries the power switch, the USB-C port and four 3.5 mm jacks — audio out, multi-out, MIDI in and audio in.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/hardware-overview#inputs-outputs",{"id":149,"text":150,"source":147,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"mic-and-meter","A small built-in microphone and a vertical LED level meter sit in the top right margin.",{"id":152,"text":153,"source":154,"firmware_min":21,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"battery","Holding `com` turns the level meter into a rough battery gauge.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.36",[156,163,170,178,185,193,200,207],{"id":157,"goal":158,"preconditions":159,"steps":160,"result":23,"source":39,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"switch-mode","Switch to another main mode",[],[161],{"keys":162,"note":23,"set":23},"instrument/auxiliary/arrange/mix",{"id":164,"goal":165,"preconditions":166,"steps":167,"result":23,"source":44,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"open-page","Open one of the current mode's module pages",[],[168],{"keys":169,"note":23,"set":23},"M1…M4",{"id":171,"goal":172,"preconditions":173,"steps":174,"result":23,"source":44,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"shift-page","Show the shift-layer parameters of the current page",[],[175],{"keys":176,"note":177,"set":23},"hold shift","the extra parameters stay while shift is down",{"id":179,"goal":180,"preconditions":181,"steps":182,"result":23,"source":54,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"select-track","Choose the track to edit",[],[183],{"keys":184,"note":23,"set":23},"T1…T8",{"id":186,"goal":187,"preconditions":188,"steps":190,"result":23,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"restart","Restart playback from the top of the pattern",[189],"playback is running",[191],{"keys":192,"note":23,"set":23},"play",{"id":194,"goal":195,"preconditions":196,"steps":197,"result":23,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"silence","Stop and silence everything",[],[198],{"keys":199,"note":23,"set":23},"stop → stop",{"id":201,"goal":202,"preconditions":203,"steps":204,"result":23,"source":62,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"octave","Move the keyboard an octave down or up",[],[205],{"keys":206,"note":23,"set":23},"[-]/[+]",{"id":152,"goal":208,"preconditions":209,"steps":210,"result":23,"source":154,"firmware_min":21,"verified_on":23,"confidence":40},"Check the battery level",[],[211],{"keys":212,"note":213,"set":23},"hold com","read the level meter in the top right margin",[],[216,217],"sequencer.step-components","com.midi-settings","The OP-XY packs everything into one flat grid of square keys, so a few landmarks make it easy to\nfind your way. The left block is about _where you are_: the four mode keys (`instrument`,\n`auxiliary`, `arrange`, `mix`) and, below them, the transport. The middle is about _what you edit_:\nthe module keys `M1`…`M4` under the screen choose a page, the track keys under the encoders choose a\ntrack, and the step keys below them are the sequencer. The right-hand column holds the utility keys\n(`sample`, `com`, `player`, `bar`).\n\nMost editing follows one pattern: pick a mode, pick a track, pick a page, then `turn E1`…`E4`.\n`shift` reaches a second layer of almost every key and page, and the keyboard's white and black keys\ndouble as step-component and number keys when a page asks for them.",[220,222,224,225,226,227,228,229,230,231,232,233,234,235,236,237,238,239,240,241,242,243,244],{"url":28,"kind":221},"research",{"url":39,"kind":223},"guide",{"url":44,"kind":223},{"url":54,"kind":223},{"url":58,"kind":223},{"url":62,"kind":223},{"url":72,"kind":221},{"url":77,"kind":221},{"url":87,"kind":221},{"url":99,"kind":223},{"url":103,"kind":223},{"url":107,"kind":223},{"url":111,"kind":223},{"url":115,"kind":223},{"url":119,"kind":223},{"url":123,"kind":223},{"url":127,"kind":223},{"url":131,"kind":223},{"url":135,"kind":223},{"url":139,"kind":223},{"url":143,"kind":223},{"url":147,"kind":223},{"url":154,"kind":245},"changelog",[247,248,249,250,251,252,253,254,255,256,257,258,259,260,261,262,263,264,265,266,267,268],"key.instrument","key.auxiliary","key.arrange","key.mix","key.m1","key.m2","key.m3","key.m4","key.shift","track.1","track.2","track.3","track.4","track.5","track.6","track.7","track.8","key.play","key.stop","key.minus","key.plus","key.com",{"id":10,"title":270},"Hardware",{"id":272,"title